course: dictionary
lesson: 10850
title: One word, many meanings: vessel
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one you need. Vessel is one of these words. Read the clues around it before you choose.
explain: «It squeezes about 70 to 100 times a minute and pumps blood through tubes called blood vessels.» The clues are blood and tubes, so here a vessel is a tube that carries blood around the body.
explain: «The sailing vessel crossed the sea before the storm.» Here the clue is sailing, so a vessel is a ship. Check your choice by swapping in your meaning. Only the meaning that fits the clues will make sense.
fact: Vessel is a noun, and it has more than one meaning.
fact: A vessel can be a ship or a large boat, as in «sailing vessel» and «fishing vessel».
fact: A vessel can be a container for liquids, like a cup, bowl, jug or barrel; this meaning is old-fashioned or formal, as in «a vessel of water».
fact: A blood vessel is a tube that carries blood around the body: arteries, veins and capillaries are all blood vessels.
fact: In a plant, a vessel is a tube that carries water and food.
exercise: «The fishing vessel left the harbour at dawn.» What is a vessel here? | A tube in the body | *A ship or large boat | A bowl for soup | A seed in the soil
exercise: «The heart pumps blood through vessels to every part of the body.» What are the vessels in this sentence? | *Tubes that carry blood | Large boats on the sea | Glass jars for water | Leaves that catch sunlight
exercise: «Fish take oxygen from water with gills, thin feathery parts full of blood vessels.» Which meaning of vessel fits here? | A ship sailing across the sea | A bowl used in the kitchen | A jug for pouring water | *A tube that carries blood
test: Sam says a vessel is always a boat. Is he right? | Yes, a vessel is always a boat | Yes, a vessel is always a bowl | Yes, but only in science lessons | *No, a vessel can also be a tube in the body or a container
test: «A bump on the head swells because the scalp has many blood vessels that leak under the skin.» What does vessels mean here? | Roots that hold soil | *Tubes that carry blood | Ships at sea | Cups for drinks
exam: «The elephant's ears are full of blood vessels that help cool the blood.» What does vessels mean here? | Jugs for water | Ships that sail the sea | *Tubes that carry blood | Pots for plants
